<code>assert c != null => this.equals(new Vector<>(c));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.equals(new Vector<>(c));</code>

However, since the comment specifies that the vector should be equal to the collection `c`, and given the `equals` method's contract, we should compare `this` vector to `c` directly:

<code>assert c != null => this.equals(c);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.equals(new Vector<>(c));</code>
--------------------
